@reranker/catalog

The place names in data/geo (Spanish names, local names and aliases of regions and cities
outside Colombia) and the centroids of those regions and cities are derived from the GeoNames
geographical database, https://www.geonames.org, a project of Unxos GmbH, licensed under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

Changes: scripts/build-geo.ts pairs GeoNames entries with DataForSEO's Google locations and
keeps, per place, one display name, a few aliases and the entry's coordinates, taken from
admin1CodesASCII.txt, admin2Codes.txt, cities500.txt, allCountries.txt, alternateNamesV2.txt
and countryInfo.txt. The files used, with their date and SHA-256, are listed under
sourceGeoNames in data/geo/manifest.json.

The data is provided by GeoNames "as is", without warranty of any kind.

The Swiss language areas in data/regional-languages.json are derived from the Swiss Federal
Statistical Office (BFS/OFS), Application of Swiss Communes, typologies SPRGEB2020 and
SPRGEB2000, https://www.agvchapp.bfs.admin.ch, under the BFS open-use terms (source must be
cited). Each place is joined to its canton through the Google Ads geotargets file,
https://developers.google.com/google-ads/api/data/geotargets. scripts/build-regional-languages.ts
lists the files used with their SHA-256 in the output.
